==Finnish==

===Etymology===
Originally meaning "glutton (one who eats a lot)", from {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*ahma}}. Related to dialectal {{cog|et|ahm}}, {{cog|izh|ahmo}}, {{cog|krl|ahmo}}, {{m|krl|ahmoi}}, {{cog|lud|ahmo}}, {{cog|vot|ahmia}} (~ {{m|fi|ahmia}}) and more distantly to {{cog|se|vuosmmis}} (from {{cog|smi-pro|*vuosvēs}}).

The meaning "wolverine" is possibly a calque from other European languages such as {{ncog|de|Vielfraß}} and {{ncog|la|gulo}}.

